Package: landform
Title: Topographic Position Index-Based Landform Classification
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Gianmarco", "Alberti", email = "gianmarcoalberti@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Classifies a landscape into slope-position and landform classes on the
    basis of the Topographic Position Index (TPI) and slope, following
    Weiss (2001, Topographic Position and Landforms Analysis, ESRI User
    Conference) and Jenness (2006, TPI extension for ArcView 3.x). Two
    classifications are offered: a six-class Slope Position
    Classification, based on one TPI scale, and a ten-class Landform
    Classification, based on a small and a large TPI scale. The TPI can be
    computed over square, circular or annular neighbourhoods, sized in
    cells or in map units, and standardised either over the whole grid (as
    in the original method) or locally. Results are returned as an object
    holding the classified raster, the TPI and slope surfaces, and
    per-class descriptive statistics, with methods for printing,
    summarising and plotting.
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    graphics,
    grDevices,
    terra (>= 1.7-3)
Suggests:
